  "title": "Unified 3D Saliency Field for 2D-3D Localization",
  "summary": "This paper proposes a continuous 3D saliency field derived from 2D detector responses, which improves 2D-3D localization by enhancing detectability at any 3D point near a surface. The field is queried in a 3D space and used as a viewpoint utility to estimate image detection, surpassing existing methods in both object recognition and real-world scenarios.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "DetField is a continuous 3D saliency field that predicts image detectability at any 3D point near a surface.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "DetField outperforms Harris-3D and five learned 3D keypoint methods on objects and real indoor scenes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "DetField improves localization success by 7.4 points on unseen rooms compared to Harris-3D.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
